Time Complexity of Factorial Program

Case          	Complexity	
Best Case	        O(n)	
Average Case    	O(n)	
Worst Case	      O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Conclusion:

The factorial program calculates the factorial of a given number n by initializing factorial to 1 and repeatedly multiplying it by each integer from 1 to n using a for loop.
The time complexity is O(n) because the loop executes exactly n times. The auxiliary space complexity is O(1) because only a fixed number of variables are used.
Therefore, the iterative factorial algorithm is a simple and efficient method for calculating the factorial of a number.
